in-step durations come from the timed window only: true
a later routine's segments map to the table's indices after its predecessors': true
the isolated warmup run is not an isolated timing: true
ISO flags an isolated time off its in-step one, SPREAD a wide in-step spread: true
with a common factor of 1, OWN flags exactly what ISO does: true
one cell renders its table and owes no repeatability section: true
cells of one kernel list are compared kernel by kernel, the moved one listed: true
a cell that shipped other kernels is attributed but compared with none: true
a step-wide clock factor is ISO but not OWN; a kernel's own deviation beyond it is: true
the report states the factor, its per-step spread and the OWN share: true
without enough sizeable kernels there is no factor, and OWN flags nothing: true
a rocprofv3 kernel trace attributes as the nsys export does: true
a HIP cell's attribution states its memory model and its tracer: true
a HIP cell that states no memory model: refused
a HIP cell whose kernels ran on two agents: refused
a cell with two trace exports: refused
an incomplete table, a missing trace or result, a short window, an unmapped segment: refused
a report with a refused cell, or with no cell, fails: true
